L490: Protocol deviations which are found to frequently recur, will
L491: require (immediate) action. Protocol violations will also
L492: require a documented “Corrective Action Preventive Action
L493: (CAPA)” plan.
L494: Investigator acknowledges that such recurring protocol
L495: deviations could potentially be classified as a serious
L496: violation. his understood that “a serious violation” is likely
L497: to affect to a significant degree:
L498:                                                                 - the safety or physical or mental integrity of the
L499: Trial participants; or
L500:                                                                 - the scientific validity of the Trial
L501: The Investigator is expected to take immediate action
L502: required to protect the safety of the trial participant(s),
L503: even if this action represents a deviation from the protocol.
L504: In such cases, the CI/Sponsor should be notified of this
L505: action and the EC at the Trial site should be informed
L506: according to local procedures and applicable regulations.
L507: The impact of deviations/violations and/or missing data on
L508: the study results will be assessed by the Pl and
L509: statistician. Handling of such deviations and/or data gaps
L510: will be described in the Statistical Analysis Plan (SAP) by
L511: the statistician. The statistician will alert the PI/study
L512: team/CTC Data Manager/Monitor (as appropriate), of any
L513: non-compliance issues that significantly impact the data
L514: integrity and/or validity of the study data (e.g. issues that
L515: introduce potential bias or that compromise the study
L516: endpoints).
