L521: establish randomization / treatment albocation; or refer to the final, approved protocol 1f detailed information
L522: is available there.
L523: The trail randomization is described in section 7.3 of the protocol.
L524: To ensure the integrity of the trial, randomization through a computerized system has been established. A
L525: randomization kit list will be generatecl by ARDENA Gent NV and uploaded into www.randornize.net.
L526: Randomization will happen ina 1:1 allocation ratio stratified by site. Patients in the trial will be randomly
L527: assigned to the intervention group or the control group. Within each site, block randomization will be
L528: applied using varying block size The total number of blocks is 90, and the number of treatment numbers is
L529: between 001- 360.
L530: www.randomize.net is a web based system and accessible 24/7. Each apphicable study site staff member
L531: will have a personal log in for randomization.
L532: When the patient has been randomized in www.randomize.net, a patient treatment kit number will be
L533: allocated. The apphicable stucly site staff members will receive this kit number via mail.
L534: Blinding, packaging and distribution of IMP is described in section 7.4 of the protocol:
L535: These pre-made kits will contain the bhinded IV ampoules for the entire treatment period (16 doses -4 days)
L536: for the patient.
L537: The treatment kit will contain 52 (4 back-up) ampoules of Vitamin C SOOmg/5ml OR 52 ampoules of Normal
L538: Sahine 5m1 9mg/mI. These ampoules have identicah sizes and will be blinded by a cap and sticker so that
L539: they look identical. For administration, bedside nurses will have to dilute 3 ampoules in Sürnl of Normal
