L616: 1. DATA RETENTION, CONTINGENCY & DISASTER RECOVERY
L617: 1.1 Describe contingency procedures and data
L618: backup schedule
L619: 1.2 Provide reference to relevant system
L620: disaster recovery procedures
L621: For the UZL REDCap database, the following KiJ Leuven
L622: procedures for system recovery apply:
L623: - Systems are proactively monitored 24 hours a day, 7
L624: days a week.
L625: - An emergency on-calI service guarantees constant
L626: monitoring
L627: of the technical equipment, also outside
L628: office hours, but not at night. The on-calI service is
L629: notified automatically in case of problems (between
L630: 7.00  - 23.00 hrs).
L631: - There are no fixed maintenance windows: a timely
L632: email is sent to inform the local IT Administrator of any
L633: planned maintenance or upgrades.
L634: - Any service unavailability, scheduled or unscheduled, is
L635: announced en the ICTS status page.
L636: - The web space is designed redundantly: in the event of
L637: system problems en one back-end server, all traffic is
L638: automatically diverted to another back-end server. The
L639: database plattorm is also designed redundantly.
L640: In the UZL REDCap database, data is backed up as
L641: follows:
L642: The web server backup regime is specified below:
L643: - An hourly backup, the last 6 versions of which are
L644: saved
L645: - A daily backup, the last 7 versions of which are
L646: saved
L647:      - A weekly backup, the last 6 versions of which are
L648: saved
L649:  - The database backup regime is specified below:
L650: - A nightly cold backup of all databases
L651:      - One month’s storage of the nightly cold backups
L652:  - Data restore, upon request
